{
  "category": "Bugs",
  "description": "**Fix Barcode Scanner Integration & Sparepart Edit Form Data Retrieval**\n\nRestore barcode scanning for sparepart lookup across Bengkel Transaksi and Master Data Sparepart modules, and resolve \"data sparepart tidak ditemukan\" error when opening the sparepart edit form. Compatible with mobile browsers via HTTPS.\n\n**Scope:**\n- Bengkel Transaksi (workshop transaction module)\n- Master Data Sparepart (sparepart master data list/search)\n- Sparepart Edit Form (modal or page opened from grid)\n\n---\n\n**Bug 1: Barcode Scanner Not Triggering Lookup**\n\nScanner input events are not being captured, or captured data fails to produce a DB lookup.\n\nInvestigation & Fix:\n\n1. **Input event listener** — audit `keydown`/`input` binding on scanner target fields in both modules. Ensure listeners are attached after DOM ready and survive re-renders (SPA route changes). Test focus detection: scanner must have focus before accepting input.\n\n2. **Trailing newline/CR** — scanned barcodes terminate with `\\n` or `\\r\\n`. Strip all trailing whitespace (including `\\r`, `\\n`, `\\t`) from scanned string before lookup.\n\n3. **DB lookup column** — confirm scanner sends data matching `part_number` or `barcode` column. Check for format mismatch: EAN-13, internal part codes, custom formats. Normalize string (trim, uppercase/lowercase as needed) before query.\n\n4. **QZ Tray compatibility** — if QZ Tray is deployed, validate its event bridge is correctly forwarding scan data to the web app (or bypassing it on mobile where QZ Tray is absent).\n\n5. **Mobile browser HTTPS constraints** — camera-based barcode input on mobile may behave differently from hardware scanners (simulated keypress events). Verify `input` event fires correctly; test on real Android/iOS devices via HTTPS.\n\n6. **Lookup execution** — confirm the query executes on scan event (not blocked by validation, async race condition, or debounce). Log query + result for debugging.\n\n---\n\n**Bug 2: Edit Form \"Data Sparepart Tidak Ditemukan\"**\n\nThe edit form receives an identifier but the DB query returns empty.\n\nInvestigation & Fix:\n\n1. **Trace ID/UUID parameter** — map the full path from sparepart list grid → route → edit component. Check if the parameter is correctly serialized in the URL or state store.\n\n2. **Parameter type mismatch** — DB column type (int/bigint) vs route param type (string/UUID). If the column is integer but the param is a UUID string (or vice versa), the query silently fails. Cast to correct type before query.\n\n3. **Soft-delete filtering** — if the record has `deleted_at IS NOT NULL`, a default scope may exclude it. Decide: show a \"record telah dihapus\" message instead of \"data tidak ditemukan\", or restore visibility if soft-delete is only archival.\n\n4. **Permission/visibility scope** — verify the current user's role has read access to the selected sparepart. Check if a global query scope (e.g., `where('company_id', auth()->id())`) is filtering out the record.\n\n5. **State persistence after scan** — if the user arrived at edit via scan (not grid selection), verify the identifier is correctly carried through the navigation chain: scan → search result → edit link.\n\n6. **Fix the query** — ensure the edit form controller uses the correct column (`id`, `uuid`, or `barcode`) and includes/excludes soft-deleted records per requirements.\n\n---\n\n**Edge Cases (all must be handled):**\n\n| Case | Expected Behavior |\n|------|------------------|\n| Invalid/unrecognized barcode | Show user-friendly toast/alert (\"Barcode tidak dikenali\"), clear input, no crash |\n| Empty/null scan result | Ignore silently or show \"Silakan scan ulang\" |\n| Trailing whitespace/newlines | Stripped before lookup |\n| Special characters in barcode | Preserved in string, properly escaped in query |\n| Rapid continuous scans | Debounce or process sequentially, no overlap |\n| Slow manual scan vs one-shot scan | Both captured via `input` event, not timing-dependent |\n| Soft-deleted record | Show appropriate message, not generic \"not found\" |\n| Role-restricted record | Show \"akses ditolak\" if user lacks permission |\n| Mobile HTTPS autofocus | Scanner field remains focused after camera input; refocus if lost |\n\n---\n\n**Verification Checklist (post-fix):**\n\n1. Scan valid barcode in Bengkel Transaksi → sparepart data auto-populates fields\n2. Scan valid barcode in Master Data Sparepart → search result displays correctly\n3. Open edit form from grid → full sparepart data loads, no error\n4. Open edit form after scan → same result\n5. Scan invalid barcode → error toast, no crash\n6. Scan barcode with trailing `\\r\\n` → works same as clean scan\n7. Test on mobile Chrome/Safari via HTTPS — all flows work\n8. Verify lookup latency < 500ms (perception target)\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Access to sparepart DB schema (confirm `part_number`, `barcode`, `deleted_at` columns)\n- QZ Tray version + config if deployed\n- Real mobile device(s) for HTTPS testing (Android + iOS)",
