    {
      "description": "Fix Barcode Scanner Integration & Sparepart Edit Form Data Retrieval\n\n**Scope:** Workshop transaction module (bengkel transaksi), sparepart master data module (master-data sparepart), sparepart edit form.\n\n**Two bugs:**\n1. Barcode scanner non-functional in both modules (no scan trigger, no lookup, no data population)\n2. Edit sparepart form fails to open: \"data sparepart tidak ditemukan\" error\n\n**Root cause investigation required:**\n\n- **Barcode scanner (both modules):** Inspect scanner input event handling, focus detection, scan-to-input binding. Check for trailing newlines/CR in scanned data, compatibility with QZ Tray (if applicable), and barcode format mismatch (EAN-13, internal codes, etc.) vs DB lookup field (part_number / barcode column). Verify lookup logic executes correctly on scan.\n\n- **Edit form \"data not found\":** Trace ID/UUID parameter passed from sparepart list to edit form route. Check DB query logic — likely mismatch between parameter type (string vs int), soft-deleted record filtering, permission/visibility scope, or stale data after scan selection. Verify state persistence between master-data grid and edit modal/page.\n\n**Fix requirements:**\n- Restore barcode scanner → sparepart lookup → field population in bengkel transaksi\n- Restore barcode scanner → sparepart search/display in master-data sparepart\n- Fix edit form data retrieval so \"data sparepart tidak ditemukan\" no longer appears\n- Ensure edit form loads with correct, complete sparepart data\n\n**Edge cases to cover:**\n- Invalid or unrecognized barcodes (show appropriate error, no crash)\n- Various barcode formats (EAN, internal codes, slow manual scan vs rapid scan)\n- Null/empty scan results\n- Soft-deleted or filtered sparepart records\n- Role-based access restrictions\n- Trailing whitespace/newlines in scanned input\n- Special characters in barcode strings\n- Post-fix: verify end-to-end flow (scan → find → open edit → display details)",
